      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Continuous variables were pooled as mean difference (MD) and 95% confidence interval (CI) using inverse variance method. Mortality was analyzed using the Mantel-Haenszel (M-H) method to calculate odds ratio (OR) and 95% confidence interval (CI).",
      "reason": "The Statistical Analysis section specifies effect measures for each outcome type: MD for continuous variables, OR via Mantel-Haenszel for mortality, and log ORs from Cox models via generic inverse variance for PCT predicting mortality. Results also report RR and HR (text_14, text_5)."
    },
